<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: AIB, Guardian PMPA to cross-sell products.</title>
<headline>AIB, Guardian PMPA to cross-sell products.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allied Irish Banks Plc and Guardian PMPA said on Monday they had reached agreement on a deal to cross sell insurance and banking products to their respective customers.</p>
<p>&quot;The new arrangement will allow each company to provide enhanced service and value to its own customers, and the first new product offerings are likely to be launched in the autumn,&quot; Guardian PMPA said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
